# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the Airflow webserver ALREADY RUNNING with the
# vulnerable default secret_key (temporary_key) loaded, then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the webserver is signing session cookies with the default key when the
#     agent starts, which makes the "changed secret_key but never restarted the
#     webserver" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the webserver cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART the webserver after changing
# secret_key, not merely edit airflow.cfg.
